  "claim": "The box set Live from the Atlantic Studios was by the Australian band who recorded the song \"Let's Get It Up\". It included a remastered version of this live album. It was produced by Robert John \"Mutt\" Lange.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Bonfire (album). Sentence: Bonfire is a five-disc box set by Australian band AC/DC, released in 1997, and remastered with a release in Digipak format in 2003.\nPage: Bonfire (album). Sentence: It was created as a tribute to the band's earlier singer Bon Scott and included the two disc soundtrack to the movie \"Let There Be Rock\", some early unreleased tracks, a live recording from the Atlantic Records studio in New York and a remastered version of \"Back in Black\".\nPage: Back in Black. Sentence: Produced by Robert John \"Mutt\" Lange, the album was released on 25 July 1980 by Albert Productions and Atlantic Records.\nPage: Live from the Atlantic Studios. Sentence: Live from the Atlantic Studios is a live album by AC/DC released on the \"Bonfire\" box set.\nPage: Let's Get It Up. Sentence: \"Let's Get It Up\" is a song by Australian hard rock band AC/DC, first released on their 1981 album \"For Those About to Rock We Salute You\", and later as its first single.",
